28216" :question/problem "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=2v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=2.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-328216/field-1" "q-328216/field-2" "q-328216/field-3" "q-328216/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "166cd7e4-5568-5769-8bc6-4ffc4ed8b508"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-328216"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-78295/selection/ea817ba85a431474579f60c763d2b8780134573250538e3dcbb7bc386fc9864e" :answer/id #uuid "adef0d61-23f2-51ea-ad40-21e962d34517" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78295/selection/e0277fd89262e5baaa9a94c159184eaacf31a4c0b99e286b9b68023aa3437c11" :answer/id #uuid "8bfedff4-0355-5b91-b95c-50340f09a459" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{9} \\\\ \\frac{1}{9} & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-78295/selection/f77a844802db4e1332b62dc88fa77ea284627b11d7281b58a1672b01da168bb3" :answer/id #uuid "ecd3f596-3b12-5df1-87e0-6df036d5ba71"